{"ts":"2026-07-27T04:55:32.943Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-slack-e78x"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"slack notify, slack test, and slack digest fail to register on pm-cli 2026.7.27 because they redeclare the host-owned --json global"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"pm-cli 2026.7.27 (GH-719) makes the host reject any extension command whose flags shadow a host-owned global. slack notify, slack test, and slack digest each declared { long: \"--json\" }, so registerCommand threw and all three commands failed to register against a real host. The suite never caught it because every smoke test asserted against a hand-rolled api double that accepts all registrations unconditionally. Fix: drop the flag declarations, read ctx.global.json, and rebuild the smoke suite on the SDK createExtensionTestHarness so pm's real activation engine validates registration."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-27T04:55:32.943Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-27T04:55:32.943Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-agent"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"cf332701fc3a6bc227c01e570c00c328368b195a11b527b1b514dd7b2c4e8513","message":""}
